{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:05Z","created_by_operation":"op_13e68b81831c469e9684c751cb14099f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_238efcf62959fe6a02f80350898e78bb05baac66149716872c4a09057fcd5e9c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"edantoledo/stoix@8fff19c94a47 snapshot 1747bcbd8c5bbd73","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1621dd6e4e3c827cf1675836294bd11af847d8c367ce3666644f8548a80ace86","slc_74835ee2fa5c10527f16a9ddedd764d56201a7ecb8f7e78d91cec4b19aecbf83","slc_a0adec8229e5e3c13cfbdbfc0df3cb367fb10ee80557be6ec04174eaa90ccb8d","slc_d7dd8ead017eb2eeed3d5eac4b3dc755245c4297ea75f926a1ec871cacbd59a0","slc_fbc91a8fd189f20d62cb84a9f223872e32efad64936a8b500757b058a46fd58c"],"source_ids":["src_6a524f0af5dc5d31b18f635c5f63b20d"],"text":"JaxARC environment integration exposes four ARC datasets (Mini, AGI1, AGI2, ConceptARC), three action modes (point, bbox, mask), and domain metrics like best_similarity and solved via an ExtendedMetrics wrapper.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:05Z","updated_by_operation":"op_13e68b81831c469e9684c751cb14099f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:05Z","created_by_operation":"op_13e68b81831c469e9684c751cb14099f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3ef53f9cc74098873b3d5cbb5ca09a62d2db7e3f3deacd3c20ad8fee960eecea","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"edantoledo/stoix@8fff19c94a47 snapshot 1747bcbd8c5bbd73","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1d3687974b4df634690c3d11c9db1ad681e5f0ab7e62a63adc8c9fd6c35fca77","slc_22b1db7be458f342a1c646aee4b00782d0098d717cbed79f4dd6a660a4a1d6cc","slc_43de5e0221514bf97498ab2561809c045372584036520e40e2fb9433435e036f","slc_4ff8004513fbe1f8f084cf49bc96f571608ecaf91e612634a6a21c61b2260e48","slc_991569bed48048638899fe56ee7f8e5fbe20f4c81075457d6abba6fe4a6b5983"],"source_ids":["src_f6e426d3c37d5cf29d2d5a76be304ac3"],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors must sign a Contributor License Agreement, use prefixed hyphen-delimited branch names, follow conventional commits, install pre-commit hooks, and submit all changes via GitHub pull request review.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:05Z","updated_by_operation":"op_13e68b81831c469e9684c751cb14099f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:05Z","created_by_operation":"op_13e68b81831c469e9684c751cb14099f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_439a9f8ce5eb284dae42d79c7babeaacdd3293c6e77d5c52052200d0bc569339","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"edantoledo/stoix@8fff19c94a47 snapshot 1747bcbd8c5bbd73","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_46264f23e454c38fc1bc5134a40b628117fc77db525fb2a3230f147f90934637","slc_e8b0ca30d8fa1e5c8da3ec78dc1dc32b279d281864b70dddb95f7c8740239fbf"],"source_ids":["src_2c2ae8d2667356cf88e06a02262b58fc"],"text":"Stoix is intentionally not a modular importable library; it follows a CleanRL/PureJaxRL-style philosophy allowing code duplication for readability, with abstraction used for networks, environments, logging, and evaluation.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:05Z","updated_by_operation":"op_13e68b81831c469e9684c751cb14099f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:05Z","created_by_operation":"op_13e68b81831c469e9684c751cb14099f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4a812e86ebe9ba196d3b3d016ea96420b250f0aa86d210aafff1e5f79d308b6d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"edantoledo/stoix@8fff19c94a47 snapshot 1747bcbd8c5bbd73","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_9af3f99e284f1118c795a46013123fd24e0a9482dd50683e4e8735d1cdbbd675","slc_c49b3ad7531b079a8e80a436a2bbfe0212df963cd26b0c74628248a5362dbd3f"],"source_ids":["src_2c2ae8d2667356cf88e06a02262b58fc"],"text":"The repository provides single-file implementations of many popular RL algorithms, including DQN variants, Rainbow, R2D2, DDPG family, TD3, SAC, PPO, DPO, and MPO.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:05Z","updated_by_operation":"op_13e68b81831c469e9684c751cb14099f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:05Z","created_by_operation":"op_13e68b81831c469e9684c751cb14099f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6d8730257a673a97941c703f11ad383c3d54d352fba3971556aea31ffb7f4466","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"edantoledo/stoix@8fff19c94a47 snapshot 1747bcbd8c5bbd73","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_c49b3ad7531b079a8e80a436a2bbfe0212df963cd26b0c74628248a5362dbd3f"],"source_ids":["src_2c2ae8d2667356cf88e06a02262b58fc"],"text":"All implementations include checkpointing to save and resume parameters and training runs, and training can be vectorized with vmap on one device or distributed with pmap across devices.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:05Z","updated_by_operation":"op_13e68b81831c469e9684c751cb14099f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:05Z","created_by_operation":"op_13e68b81831c469e9684c751cb14099f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8bb24a521188826aab2a446c388007d3ee752b75196261629cb9f59ca7b6fa6b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"edantoledo/stoix@8fff19c94a47 snapshot 1747bcbd8c5bbd73","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0477e84c6be984af8b0d3d3080d15d2cbdeccf97dacfecf516ee2723c386f747","slc_87ccb49d40d32fdec0fda933959b05437fce0c244a14bf7a0b8e8533d51aa884","slc_e8c9105fa9644c6f5461d1dd509f0906c988c47eed5d17aa71aab41c3152b3ea"],"source_ids":["src_2c2ae8d2667356cf88e06a02262b58fc"],"text":"Some algorithm variants are selected purely via network architecture config, e.g. Dueling DQN or dueling C51 by passing network=mlp_dueling_dqn or mlp_dueling_c51 to the base DQN/C51 scripts.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:05Z","updated_by_operation":"op_13e68b81831c469e9684c751cb14099f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:05Z","created_by_operation":"op_13e68b81831c469e9684c751cb14099f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8c1225d3c20ef9c94434fab1b642d13c61aee0ac8ee567100732a9118126dcbb","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"edantoledo/stoix@8fff19c94a47 snapshot 1747bcbd8c5bbd73","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4a78ef69c64da64ab3790d5896ddc9a0817b659079ffd0709a11d62710081d79","slc_80aac4a89aec17c818335d06689c112db81c76eab52d460e1e75f169804ccd0b"],"source_ids":["src_2c2ae8d2667356cf88e06a02262b58fc"],"text":"Stoix includes wrappers for JAX environments such as Gymnax, Jumanji, Brax, XMinigrid, Craftax, POPJym, Navix and JaxARC, plus non-JAX environments Envpool and Gymnasium.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:05Z","updated_by_operation":"op_13e68b81831c469e9684c751cb14099f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:05Z","created_by_operation":"op_13e68b81831c469e9684c751cb14099f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9a47d3ce9d49bb9e528626eb027b4a444d3017be965e21dd7600dd3c7b87f3df","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"edantoledo/stoix@8fff19c94a47 snapshot 1747bcbd8c5bbd73","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2b86db456ce389e83a93646bdf5bd44e8e6c8191e7b424c108bda64a1fed6ec6","slc_5cfa971197b6d5cf11ec0ade36e7d110a91cd95b142dbd6edb016df422115476","slc_a35e6eab153958d723d2286af040456ef358ecd5ffc65ce1cce664cb0c9d5d17"],"source_ids":["src_2c2ae8d2667356cf88e06a02262b58fc"],"text":"A SLURM launcher built on Hydra and submitit automatically submits a separate job per algorithm/environment/seed combination, with configurable resources like partition, time, nodes, and GPUs.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:05Z","updated_by_operation":"op_13e68b81831c469e9684c751cb14099f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:05Z","created_by_operation":"op_13e68b81831c469e9684c751cb14099f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a7c783cf93a8a0ccb289eae9cf5ba9efc354592dc6daeee28dcc688c9905e6da","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"edantoledo/stoix@8fff19c94a47 snapshot 1747bcbd8c5bbd73","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0b1c4358fbd0eda910ee3d3e18b574fce106b119fe5c70f601139f1064c40e6d","slc_0d66f0f855a8d280c313330b8d5940cdaf82da4a40562b612b3e5fc5b7e433fb","slc_3f7c446721b3c051010607b51b165bb8e4da52629989b977667f6d0c0ff2da75"],"source_ids":["src_2c2ae8d2667356cf88e06a02262b58fc"],"text":"Stoix offers two system paradigms: Anakin, fully compiled end-to-end with JAX jit/pmap for native JAX environments, and Sebulba, which separates acting and learning devices and supports non-JAX environments.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:05Z","updated_by_operation":"op_13e68b81831c469e9684c751cb14099f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:05Z","created_by_operation":"op_13e68b81831c469e9684c751cb14099f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ac6d09c45b713415c41539dc56e9c8e706d8cee58052a01ffe2a88aa5455638b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"edantoledo/stoix@8fff19c94a47 snapshot 1747bcbd8c5bbd73","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_384e83aa7bfee4f89785379c08a553fcb13c9613b2b18d072d567074fc8bd9ef","slc_79833d8341f7c111bb097a1cfc4f4004dae4cf1983c2f1c25442e51a7b82c389","slc_9fcd5558b1ef18197b679e1834c3a293c0dc973d58efc206424b6fcc702b2fcc"],"source_ids":["src_2c2ae8d2667356cf88e06a02262b58fc"],"text":"Default hyperparameters and networks are not tuned for any specific environment, and the README notes actual timesteps run may be less than the requested budget unless divisibility conditions are met.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:05Z","updated_by_operation":"op_13e68b81831c469e9684c751cb14099f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:05Z","created_by_operation":"op_13e68b81831c469e9684c751cb14099f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_b568ab29f3171f66754f054300593dae3311687a1df4e09f89b4f328686c3001","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"edantoledo/stoix@8fff19c94a47 snapshot 1747bcbd8c5bbd73","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4d03e1a702e74999ec9b3e74a5843e5e52c047c005e051fc02ea1359d449685e","slc_9396d5123d170ce8964018ea2a5ebaa6743cc70fcb85c4ddeae59c176d717a51","slc_eb2219595a6487ed8612204595ddd7a8b5991f1a1ad0b527c53de60c2ba1fd50"],"source_ids":["src_2c2ae8d2667356cf88e06a02262b58fc"],"text":"Stoix targets Python 3.10, is installed by cloning and syncing with UV, and users are advised to install the JAX version matching their hardware accelerator.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:05Z","updated_by_operation":"op_13e68b81831c469e9684c751cb14099f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:05Z","created_by_operation":"op_13e68b81831c469e9684c751cb14099f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_b664691a890a2ebc1de5ee364bbbfb72163ba38ce5c88064326627cb3abff707","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"edantoledo/stoix@8fff19c94a47 snapshot 1747bcbd8c5bbd73","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_6423dd351dfe09825f09499e35fb6ca3ad66833ebe985ff7492012c1f544dbe5","slc_9fcd5558b1ef18197b679e1834c3a293c0dc973d58efc206424b6fcc702b2fcc"],"source_ids":["src_2c2ae8d2667356cf88e06a02262b58fc"],"text":"Stoix is a distributed single-agent reinforcement learning library implemented end-to-end in JAX, aimed at fast iteration on RL research ideas.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:05Z","updated_by_operation":"op_13e68b81831c469e9684c751cb14099f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:05Z","created_by_operation":"op_13e68b81831c469e9684c751cb14099f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_d7191d29a24ede4452d83a652f3b90df8611a57d7843048b85cbb88d45d62b10","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"edantoledo/stoix@8fff19c94a47 snapshot 1747bcbd8c5bbd73","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_6ba555371e3109882bd41e36a2492fbb11070923de9caf7ef85ae9c4901aa915","slc_ac44e80a7036b22ff41935f08e92bfcb345f7e73a76b7704d7ff996b6b0e8f8a","slc_f53563c3ef2187547a1848f5204f0095b22eef26fc088b2d82161eb80c570bf0"],"source_ids":["src_2c2ae8d2667356cf88e06a02262b58fc"],"text":"Systems are run as Python scripts with Hydra configuration; hyperparameters, environments, and networks can be overridden from the command line, e.g. env=gymnax/cartpole with system-level overrides.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:05Z","updated_by_operation":"op_13e68b81831c469e9684c751cb14099f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:05Z","created_by_operation":"op_13e68b81831c469e9684c751cb14099f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_dfb57a3e5085c89830e6d9afb318514243b01527433cc447da87668ea2695cdd","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"edantoledo/stoix@8fff19c94a47 snapshot 1747bcbd8c5bbd73","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_be4873f3d89a9de3b872de6079ec28186e00a2815dc40d2d379e69dfe835dc2f"],"source_ids":["src_2c2ae8d2667356cf88e06a02262b58fc"],"text":"In environments without a timestep limit or terminating mechanic, evaluation can appear to hang indefinitely while an episode never finishes; adding a step limit or action masking is suggested.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:05Z","updated_by_operation":"op_13e68b81831c469e9684c751cb14099f"}
